# EEUCC Columbus — Project Overview

## What This Project Is

A bilingual (English / Amharic) church website for **Ethiopian Emmanuel United Church of Columbus (EEUCC)**. It is a React SPA deployed to Firebase Hosting with Firestore as the database and Firebase Auth for user management.

**Live domain context:** The church is at 1055 McNaughten Rd, Columbus, OH 43213. Sunday worship is 4:00 PM – 7:00 PM.

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology | Version |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| Framework | React | 19.x |
| Build tool | Vite | 7.x |
| Routing | react-router-dom | 7.x |
| Forms | react-hook-form | 7.x |
| UI components | @headlessui/react | 2.x |
| Icons | @heroicons/react | 2.x |
| Date formatting | date-fns | 4.x |
| Backend | Firebase (Auth, Firestore, Storage, Analytics) | 12.x |
| Hosting | Firebase Hosting | — |
| CI/CD | GitHub Actions | — |
| Language | JavaScript (JSX) — **no TypeScript** | — |

## Project Structure

```
├── .github/workflows/       # CI/CD: prod deploy (main) + PR preview
├── src/
│   ├── main.jsx             # Entry point, renders <App />
│   ├── App.jsx              # BrowserRouter → AuthProvider → LanguageProvider → Routes
│   ├── App.css              # App-level overrides (dialog styles)
│   ├── index.css            # Global design system (variables, components, responsive)
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── layout/          # Layout.jsx, Navbar.jsx, Footer.jsx
│   │   └── ui/              # EventCard, SermonCard, LoadingSpinner, ProtectedRoute
│   ├── contexts/            # AuthContext.jsx, LanguageContext.jsx
│   ├── hooks/               # useFirestoreCollection, useFirestoreDoc (real-time)
│   ├── i18n/
│   │   ├── en/translations.json
│   │   └── am/translations.json
│   ├── pages/               # Home, About, Events, EventDetail, Sermons, SermonDetail,
│   │                        # Contact, Give, Login, Register, ProfileUpdate
│   └── services/            # firebase.js, authService, eventsService, sermonsService,
│                            # contactService, missingDataService
├── firebase.json            # Hosting + Firestore + Storage config
├── firestore.rules          # Security rules
├── firestore.indexes.json   # Composite indexes
├── storage.rules            # Storage security rules
├── .env.example             # Required VITE_FIREBASE_* variables
└── index.html               # SPA shell
```

## Context Providers (wrapping order)

`BrowserRouter` → `AuthProvider` → `LanguageProvider` → `AppRoutes`

## Routing

| Path | Component | Auth? |
|------|-----------|-------|
| `/` | Home | No |
| `/about` | About | No |
| `/events` | Events | No |
| `/events/:id` | EventDetail | No |
| `/sermons` | Sermons | No |
| `/sermons/:id` | SermonDetail | No |
| `/contact` | Contact | No |
| `/give` | Give | No |
| `/login` | Login (no Layout) | No |
| `/register` | Register (no Layout) | No |
| `/profile-update` | ProfileUpdate | Yes (ProtectedRoute) |
| `*` | NotFound (404) | No |

Login and Register render **outside** the Layout (no Navbar/Footer).

## Firestore Collections

| Collection | Public Read | Write |
|-----------|------------|-------|
| `users` | Own profile only | Owner creates; owner or admin updates |
| `events` | Yes | Admin only |
| `sermons` | Yes | Admin only |
| `contactMessages` | No | Anyone creates; admin manages |
| `prayerRequests` | No | Anyone creates; admin manages |
| `churchProfileUpdates` | No | Auth users create; admin manages |

## User Roles

- `member` — default role on registration, stored in `users/{uid}.role`
- `admin` — can write events/sermons, manage all collections, access admin panel

## Environment Variables

All prefixed with `VITE_FIREBASE_` and accessed via `import.meta.env`:
- `VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY`
- `VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN`
- `VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID`
- `VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET`
- `VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID`
- `VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID`
- `VITE_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID`

Optional: `VITE_CLIENT_INTAKE_FORM_URL` (Google Form embed on Contact page).

## Key Commands

```bash
npm run dev      # Start Vite dev server
npm run build    # Production build → dist/
npm run preview  # Preview production build
npm run lint     # ESLint check
```
